  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Health Systems Strenghtening for Malaria Control in Anambra and Akwa Ibom, Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project development objective is to support the State Ministries of Health in Akwa Ibom, Anambra, and Gombe states in reducing (i) malaria-related morbidity and mortality and (ii) the consequent social and economic costs.This project is funded by the Japan Social Development Fund (JSDF) to support the Malaria Control Booster Project (P097921; Additional Financing P115036). The project development objectives of the parent project are to (i) to ensure that the target population will have improved access to, and utilization of, a well-defined set of Malaria Plus Package (MPP) interventions; and (ii) to strengthen Federal and States&#x2019; ability to manage and oversee delivery of malaria plus interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
